messages.content:
value is a list of single-character strings. Return true if (), [], and {} brackets are properly nested and matched. Ignore all other characters.
Implement solve(value), taking one JSON array argument, without mutating that argument. Return only the complete replacement file in exactly one fenced python block.


Current solution.py:
```python
def solve(value):
    return value.count('(') == value.count(')') and value.count('[') == value.count(']') and value.count('{') == value.count('}')
```

